{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1846"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c154): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c154.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1846"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/countries","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__countries.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",110],["-","Asia."],["+","Asia and Africa."],["=",493],["+","In West Africa, the French colony of Upper Volta, named after the upper reaches of the Volta river, had been independent since 1960 when the young captain Thomas Sankara seized power in 1983. On 4 August 1984, the first anniversary of his revolution, he renamed it **Burkina Faso**, a hybrid of Mooré and Dioula, the country's two main languages, meaning “land of upright people”. Sankara was killed in a coup in 1987, but the name, the flag and the anthem he introduced remained.\n\n"],["=",350],["+","Upper Volta | Burkina Faso | 1984 |\n| "],["=",59]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",98],["-","Asien."],["+","Asien und Afrika."],["=",423],["+","In Westafrika war die französische Kolonie Obervolta, benannt nach dem Oberlauf des Flusses Volta, seit 1960 unabhängig, als der junge Hauptmann Thomas Sankara 1983 die Macht übernahm. Am 4. August 1984, dem ersten Jahrestag seiner Revolution, benannte er das Land in **Burkina Faso** um – eine Verbindung aus Mooré und Dioula, den beiden Hauptsprachen des Landes, die „Land der aufrechten Menschen“ bedeutet. Sankara wurde 1987 bei einem Putsch getötet, doch der Name, die Flagge und die Hymne, die er eingeführt hatte, blieben.\n\n"],["=",334],["+","Obervolta | Burkina Faso | 1984 |\n| "],["=",57]]}]},
